Z||000012||Tigger||12-18-2000||10:58 PM||||I think it would look a little better if the black side trim was painted white or you painted a black stripe around the back.<P>I know it's gota be a lot of work there. <P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Pontiaddict||12-19-2000||01:02 AM||||I like it, but if you're looking at some finishing touches...<P>You need to finish rounding off the edges of the car. For example, the top of the fastback looking from the rear has all of those squared off edges on it. (look in pic 3) As for the taillights, they need to fill more space. Other than that, filling the side strips in like you did on your green car and dropping the car 2" or so would make it look awesome. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||pHoOl||12-19-2000||01:14 AM||||Okay, some thoughts and ideas.<P>not too sure about the front, i think that it looks kinda like those jalepenos.  I like the retractable headlights, but that's just MHO.<P>as for the back.... good start.  One idea that i have looking at it is having some sort of lighting that goes the width of the panel, kinda like the late 70's T-birds, except maybe have a pegasus on each side and the pontiac in the middle.  I think that would look quite awesome.<P>there are my opinions.  you must have worked a long time on those though, and that in itself is quite admireable.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||2xsess||12-19-2000||01:37 AM||||NOt really sure what I think. Lots of work into it, that's for sure. Orville you're quite talented. I don't like the front at all. too bug-eyed for my tastes. I agree with the others about the rear tailights being too small in relation to the size of the rear end. Even something like the PONTIAC on the back of the Sunfires would help break it up.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||BOILERMAKER||12-19-2000||10:36 AM||||ONE OF A KIND!!!!!  I like it for that reason only (no harm intended).<P>Good job, I bet that took quite a bit of time!||||reg||1
Z||000017||stimpy||12-19-2000||01:46 PM||||I think it super-cool. I bet that took a LOT of work to pull off. The one thing that I think would make it even cooler would be to make a roadster out of it. I think it really fits in well with the retro vibe going around right now. <P>Hey, Orville, if you ever go up hwy 99 to SF Bay Area or Sac, stop off at my dads shop (BigO Tires, 1901 Prescott Rd, Modesto). I think he would really dig seeing this car and getting some pics. I'm sure he would cut you a deal on some wire wheels. 120 spoke knock-off Daytons in 17" would look soooo cool on that! ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Orville||12-20-2000||09:20 AM||||Thanks to all. I agree, it needs changes,<BR>especially the front. Maybe shorten the<BR>fenders, get some angles on the grill,<BR>straighten and raise the beltline. But <BR>keep the foldup lights.<BR>When time and energy permits.||||reg||1
Z||000019||mrfixit58||12-20-2000||10:37 AM||||The back reminds me of the Cadillac STS. It also has a combination of rounded and squared off edges. With it's large flat rear, it makes a great canvass to install just about any style tail lights. Something like Corvette or Late 60's GTO/69' Firebird slit tail lights would look good.<P>As for the front, it looks a little like a Buick or a Chrysler. Having the fenders stick out farther than the grill looks odd.<P>As for the grill opening... I'm having a hard time because it looks like it should have some chrome in it but, I don't think the chrome would blend with the more modern body lines. Maybe something like the new Chrysler 300. <P>What about rounding the front end like you did the rear with an little more emphases on the bottom? If you brought the bottom edge out a little further, kind of like the GT front end, the shaped the headlights more like the 240Z it may help. <P>Just some thoughts. But, I do like the effort. I wish I knew how to make that kind of stuff.<P>Keep working, <BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
